How to refer
Information for professionals
MTHC Physiotherapy helps adults aged over 18 with dizziness, vertigo, balance concerns, falls risk and movement-related symptoms to improve stability, independence and confidence in everyday life.

The service is part of MTHC’s connected care pathway and works closely with hearing care and other health services as needed.

View full referral guide →

When to referConditions we treatWhat happens after referral
Refer people aged over 18 to MTHC Physiotherapy when a person you’re seeing has:

dizziness or vertigo triggered by movement, such as turning, bending, standing or walking
signs suggesting a balance, movement or inner ear issue
unsteadiness, instability, falls risk or fear of falling
reduced confidence or daily function due to balance or movement changes
vestibular conditions where physiotherapy is recommended
neurological conditions affecting gait, balance, movement or function.
