We treat a wide range of vestibular and balance conditions using targeted assessment and evidence‑based rehabilitation.

Vestibular conditions

BPPV: current episode or post-BPPV sensitivity (people who need follow-up after repositioning)
Peripheral vestibular hypofunction: vestibular neuritis, labyrinthitis, or Ménière's disease with co-existing imbalance or BPPV
Vestibular migraine: with balance involvement
PPPD: preferably diagnosed by a neuro-otologist, though emerging presentations can begin a home exercise program while awaiting neurology review
Central vestibular dysfunction: cerebellar stroke, MS, ataxia, ABI
Balance, falls and movement concerns
We'll contact the person, confirm the booking and arrange an initial appointment.
We'll assess what's contributing to their symptoms and confirm physiotherapy is the right pathway. If referral elsewhere is more appropriate, we'll help guide that.
We'll work with the person to set clear goals and build a practical plan, whether that's a home exercise program, balance and strength work, or a combination.
